WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.562
These are the key habits from Module 10.

00:00:02.562 --> 00:00:07.167
State the grain first. Use conditional aggregation for pivots.

00:00:07.167 --> 00:00:10.252
Use UNION ALL or lateral VALUES for unpivoting.

00:00:10.252 --> 00:00:13.267
Protect the distinction between NULL and zero.

00:00:13.267 --> 00:00:15.447
Validate totals and row counts.

00:00:15.447 --> 00:00:21.377
And choose long or wide form based on the downstream task, not because one format is always better.

00:00:21.377 --> 00:00:26.652
Connect this idea to a survey project reshaping question responses for analysis.

00:00:26.652 --> 00:00:31.862
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:31.862 --> 00:00:38.982
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:38.982 --> 00:00:43.967
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:43.967 --> 00:00:49.341
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
